Category: pre-c++26. StdOptionalEmptyOptConsistency passes an empty std::optional<int> to
default_val, which formats it with CLI11's to_string: since C++26 std::optional is a range
([optional.iterators], P3168), so it is formatted as a container ("{}"), which does not convert
back to an optional<int>. The same with libstdc++ in C++26 mode (__cpp_lib_optional_range_support
is 202406L there too). The test case is left out when optional is a range.

